From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32/server/kernel32: registry values enumerate in creation order; RegGetValue REG_EXPAND_SZ sizes; mapped ini default section

Registry details the advapi32 and kernel32 conformance tests record from
Windows: RegEnumValue / NtEnumerateValueKey list a key's values in the order
they were created (the server kept them sorted by name; the sorted array is
still what lookups use, and the saved registry now writes values in creation
order, so the order survives a restart; a re-created value goes last,
overwriting keeps the place). RegGetValue of a REG_EXPAND_SZ keeps the stored
size when the expanded text is shorter and reports a size-only request for the
unexpanded value one character larger, both A and W. GetPrivateProfileSection
on an ini file mapped to the registry adds the default mapping's values to
those of the names before it instead of replacing them (it relied on the sorted
order putting the default first). Seven todo_wine marks removed from the
advapi32 registry and kernel32 profile tests.

